\begin{proof}
By hypothesis, $A$ and $B$ are closed, so $\overline{A}=A$ and $\overline{B}=B$. Since they are disjoint,
\[
A\cap\overline{B}=A\cap B=\varnothing
\quad	ext{and}
\quad
\overline{A}\cap B=A\cap B=\varnothing.
\]
Hence $A$ and $B$ are separated.
\end{proof}

